00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Let's kick off this stage of the course by confronting, honestly, the absolute biggest nightmare in product management. We're talking about terrible retention, even after a massive acquisition spend. You know the feeling, right? You pour your budget into getting users to sign up, and then they just slip right through your fingers. Ask yourself, why do some tools just effortlessly weave themselves into your daily routine, to the point where you don't even realize you're using them, while others are literally forgotten after just one single login? Like, what exactly do you do?

2
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:37.720
is the secret ingredient missing from that second group? Take a look at this number, 60%. That is a

3
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:43.140
terrifying drop-off rate. And it's exactly what Michal, a product manager at a task system called

4
00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:50.400
Velox, faced after just one single week. So why was it happening? Well, her app relied entirely on

5
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:56.120
external nudges. Think weekly reminder emails. The second those emails stopped, boom, the users

6
00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:01.020
completely vanished. So the crucial takeaway here is that you have to shift your strategy.

7
00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:06.920
You've got to move away from just buying forced engagement and instead start engineering true

8
